Goal: Maximize the points credited for completed work. Turn: Each seat completed work worth 2. Name a partner and jointly declare an amount per person (or choose -1 to file alone), then each seat submits its redemption amount. A partnership exists only when both seats name each other and declare the same amount. Scoring: Claims must equal work completed. Solo claims are checked against 2; a false solo claim pays -3. A joint invoice covers both partners, so its total authorized redemption is 4. Each partner owns half. Invalid verified claims pay -3. The third seat files independently. Rivals: Every other seat chooses its own actions and may adapt.
